  <prompt>
    Close out messaging-communication-app-r1 from the MAIN SESSION only:

    1. **README → Complete** — flip the project README status to Complete; summarize what shipped (W0–W8: ACS integration, channel provider + inbound ingestor, thread data model + `IThreadResolver`, privacy, endpoints, polling timeline + PCFs, quoting, attachments, ADR-046, docs) and the graduation criteria met (the 11 spec Success Criteria).

    2. **Lessons-learned** — author `notes/lessons-learned.md` capturing: the ACS net-new integration experience, the shared `Services/Communication/` edit (040) + characterization-guard outcome, the notification-spine coordination (threadId/kind contract for R2), the ADR-026 Path-A OOB-form+PCF surface, the NFR-04 no-client-ACS-SDK boundary, publish-size trajectory vs the ~45.30 MB baseline, and deferred items (live channel, spine push, SMS, Teams/portal, historical backfill).

    3. **`/test-diet` gate (MANDATORY, root §7)** — invoke `/test-diet` to reconcile every test added/modified during R1 (esp. task 080's vertical-slice seam + characterization tests) against the ADR-038 build-vs-maintain classifier: MAINTAIN-class tests stay at KEEP paths; SCAFFOLDING-class tests are emitted for deletion (`git rm`); AMBIGUOUS require reviewer judgment. The skill is read-only — it emits commands for the reviewer. Output: `notes/test-diet-report.md`. The wrap-up PR MUST cite this report.

    4. **Archive artifacts** — move ephemeral working files to the archive per `/repo-cleanup` conventions; retain permanent artifacts (spec, design, plan, tasks, arch docs, ADR-046).

    5. **Final `code-review`** — run a final holistic `code-review` across the R1 diff surface as a project-close quality gate (special attention to the security-sensitive privacy layer 042 + the NFR-04 no-ACS-SDK boundary).

    6. **Final TASK-INDEX reconciliation** — confirm every W0–W8 task is ✅ (or explicitly documented as deferred/owner-handoff, e.g. any PCF import handed to the owner); set `current-task.md` to "none — project complete".

    Then confirm the project is complete and ready for `merge-to-master`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke project lead running the main-session project-close protocol. Authoritative on the wrap-up sequence, the `/test-diet` gate (root §7), `/repo-cleanup`, and the final `code-review` gate. Does NOT delegate to subagents (root §3 write boundary).
  </role>

  <goal>
    README status is Complete; `notes/lessons-learned.md` and `notes/test-diet-report.md` exist; the `/test-diet` gate has run and its report is cited; ephemeral artifacts are archived; a final `code-review` has run with Critical findings addressed; TASK-INDEX is fully reconciled; `current-task.md` is "none — project complete". The project is ready to merge to master.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      This is the project-close task. Per root §7, a `090-wrapup-*` task invokes `/test-diet` BEFORE marking the project complete — reconciling R1's test additions against the ADR-038 KEEP-path categories (task 080's seam + characterization tests are the bulk). R1 was substantial (net-new ACS transport + inbound seam + thread model + security-sensitive privacy layer + client polling surface), so lessons-learned and the final review are substantive. The notification-spine coordination (threadId/kind contract) is R2-facing — record it for the sibling project.
    </background>
